  "seen": [
    "Native node field pointers stay valid across nested events, body replacement, title replacement, clear, and widget destruction.",
    "The native dispatch keeps the already allocated text buffers until the oldest scope that observes them returns. It creates neither a copy of the text nor a heap allocation to retain it.",
    "The compiler emits native event registration and a scoped read of pNode. A null node stays null, stored views expire, and explicitly read strings remain usable.",
    "String field copies report allocation failure and the next read can succeed. Renderer regressions exercise its scoped views and failure contracts."
